text=['# Actual reference-frame study\n\nThis is the evidence set for V2. Each selected image was extracted from the repository MP4, then visually inspected. Eight overview frames per source establish broad coverage; curated frames below are not a census of all visual devices. Read the source timestamp as primary identity. Legacy state IDs are lookup results only and can be wrong. The fingerprint lists confirmed conflicts.\n\n**59 curated frames; 14 sources; 8 portrait, 6 landscape.** All 14 raw overview sheets, per-source motion sample sheets, and original forensic image selections remain in `evidence/`. R01 is unused.\n\nMotion notes distinguish observed multi-frame changes from unknown exact entrances/exits. Narration excerpts are inherited ASR/sync evidence and may contain transcription errors; their timestamps were not independently forced-aligned here. The image often illustrates an analogy or consequence rather than the literal current sentence.\n']
for s in ss:
 rid=s['id']; es=[e for e in ee if e['reference']==rid];assert len(es)==len(notes[rid]),rid
 text.append(f'## {rid} — {s["slug"]}\n\n**Source video:** [{Path(s["source"]).name}](<{s["source"]}>)\n\n**Format:** {s["width"]}×{s["height"]}; {"PORTRAIT PRIORITY" if s["height"]>s["width"] else "landscape: borrow grammar, recompose for 9:16"}; {s["duration"]:.3f} s.\n\n[All eight overview frames](evidence/{rid}_overview.jpg) · [Targeted motion sequence](evidence/{rid}_motion.jpg)\n\n{style[rid]}\n\n**Observed motion study:** {motions[rid]}\n')
 for e,n in zip(es,notes[rid]):
  comp,illus,why,dens,col=n; rel=Path(e['file']).relative_to(r);speech=' / '.join(x['TEXT'] for x in e['speech']) or 'No covering sentence in inherited alignment; do not fabricate a precise word trigger.'
  text.append(f'### {e["id"]} — {e["timestamp"]:.3f} s\n\n[Open actual frame]({rel})\n\n- **SOURCE VIDEO:** {rid}, filename linked above.\n- **TIMESTAMP / STATE ID:** {e["timestamp"]:.3f} s, review frame {e["id"]}. Legacy time lookup: {e["state"]}; unverified mapping, not authority.\n- **WHY IT MATTERS:** {why}\n- **COMPOSITION:** {comp}\n- **ILLUSTRATION LANGUAGE:** {illus}\n- **COLOR USAGE / BACKGROUND:** {col}\n- **LINE LANGUAGE / TEXT USAGE:** {style[rid]}\n- **ASSET DENSITY:** {dens}\n- **MOTION INTO / OUT OF FRAME:** See observed sequence above. A still establishes this state only; exact entry/exit mechanics for this particular timestamp are not inferred from the still or a conflicting legacy row.\n- **NARRATION RELATIONSHIP:** {why} Inherited timed sentence: “{speech}” Treat this as alignment context, not proof that every word is rendered literally.\n')
text.append('## Existing forensic evidence inspected\n\nThese retained files provide an independent earlier extraction trail. Contact-sheet thumbnails establish broad scene sequence; newly extracted individual MP4 frames are used for the close visual claims.\n')
for x in json.loads((r/'evidence/forensic_files.json').read_text()):text.append(f'- {x["reference"]}: [{Path(x["path"]).name}](<{Path(x["path"]).resolve()}>)')
text.append('\n\n## Coverage and exclusions\n\nHumans/furniture: R02, R08, R09. Numbers/comparisons: R02, R05, R10, R12–R14. Danger/instability/reaction: R09, R11, R13. Transformations: R04, R05, R07, R11, R12. Scale: R03, R05, R13, R14. Payoffs: R02, R04, R06, R09, R15. No furniture or clinical instability precedent is invented for a video that does not contain it. No inspected source directly demonstrates the chair-stand test.\n\nAll V2 medical-scene metaphors are new creative decisions. Reference evidence establishes visual construction and explanatory behavior, not clinical validity. The supplied script is retained; no normative score is added.\n')
(r/'REFERENCE_FRAME_STUDY.md').write_text('\n'.join(text))
print('wrote',len(ee),'frame entries')
